nodecode-hermes-herald is a rewrite of bennybuoy's bennybuoy/hermes-herald:

  https://github.com/bennybuoy/hermes-herald
  commit 1d185a9e0f4fbfa141447be401903cc80407e1cb
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Ben Kamholtz (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's dispatch surface against one Hermes Agent API server —
dispatch_agent (POST /v1/runs, returning the run id), check_dispatch and
collect_dispatches (GET /v1/runs/{id}, several in one call), cancel_dispatch
(POST /v1/runs/{id}/stop), ping_profile (GET /v1/health), list_profile_models
(GET /v1/models, with the route/alias/parent reading that separates a
dispatchable alias from the profile's primary identity), dispatch_chat
(POST /v1/chat/completions, keeping one target session per profile), and
dispatch_status (the local record of what was dispatched from here), with their
argument schemas, their answer shapes, the run-id rules, and the model
provenance a dispatch carries. The Python (urllib, threads, SQLite) is Common
Lisp here: nlk:http for the profile's API server, one section declaration for
the settings, six nlk:define-contract declarations for the tools' arguments,
and a JSON record under the Nodecode home in place of the SQLite ledger. Where
the plugin configured many profiles and named one per call, the cell's section
names one address, because a Nodecode home talks to the profiles it is pointed
at rather than holding a roster.

Left out: delegate_subagent and llm_call, which ran a worker inside the Hermes
process against Hermes's own parent-agent context and provider routing — a
different organism's in-process seams, with the per-call model switch,
inherited context and SOUL.md those depend on. llm_direct, a second tool that
spoke to any configured OpenAI-compatible endpoint with its own key, also
needs Hermes's provider plumbing and gave a user no Hermes-specific value a
plain provider cell does not. The approval relay (approve_dispatch) and the
SSE callback listener are left out for the same reason: both delivered events
into a live Hermes session while a run went on, and a cell answering a tool
call has no session of the other process to deliver into — the run id and a
poll carry the same facts without the listener. The stamped trace/hop routing
envelope for detached graphs of dispatches is not reproduced either: the cell
dispatches to one address, so there is no graph to route.
